+## Application Execution, 2026-10-02
+
+The retained release APK installed successfully with an update installation on
+emulator-5560, Android API 37, x86_64 and actual 16 KiB pages. Its normal
+`com.azurekiln.qfli.script/.MainActivity` entry was used throughout.
+
+1. Created the isolated `LuaNativeAudit` Lua project from the ordinary UI.
+2. Ran its default `src/main.lua`: `Hello, QFLIStudio+!`, exit code 0.
+3. Invoked the editor's native syntax check: `main.lua` was valid.
+4. Invoked native compilation: generated `src/main.luac` successfully.
+5. Replaced the source with `dofile[[src/main.luac]]` and ran again. The VM
+   loaded the retained bytecode and printed the same output, exit code 0.
+
+The APK was not rebuilt or replaced with a probe target. The compiled output
+was generated by the actual app's native Lua toolchain and loaded in a later
+run. ARM device checks and Apple execution remain separate unverified gates.
